## DESCRIPTION
## Higher order derivatives
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject('Calculus - multivariable')
## DBchapter('Differentiation of multivariable functions')
## DBsection('Higher order derivatives')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros("PGstandard.pl", "PGML.pl", "MathObjects.pl");

TEXT(beginproblem());

BEGIN_PGML


The chain rule gets messy with higher order derivatives. It's mostly just tedious and will require a little more practice. Let [` f: \mathbb{R}^2 \to \mathbb{R}^3 `] and [` g: \mathbb{R}^3 \to \mathbb{R} `] be given by

>>[` f(s,t) = \left(st, 2s+3t+7, s^2+(t-1)^2\right) \qquad \text{and} \qquad g(x,y,z) = 3x+z. `]<<

Abusing notation, denote [` u = g(x,y,z) = 3x+z `] and write

>>[` x = f_1(s,t) = st, \qquad y = f_2(s,t) = 2s+3t+7,  \qquad z =  f_3(s,t) = s^2 + (t-1)^2. `]<<

Thus, [` u = g \circ f (s,t) `]. Recall by the chain rule,

>>[` \dfrac{\partial u}{\partial s} = \dfrac{\partial u}{\partial x}\dfrac{\partial x}{\partial s} + \dfrac{\partial u}{\partial y}\dfrac{\partial y}{\partial s} + \dfrac{\partial u}{\partial z}\dfrac{\partial z}{\partial s}. `]<<

Express [` \dfrac{\partial^2 u}{\partial s^2} `] in terms of other "intermediate" partial derivatives and then evaluate it at [` (s,t) = (0,0) `].

[` \dfrac{\partial^2 u}{\partial s^2}(0,0) = `] [________]{Real(2)}

Express [` \dfrac{\partial^2 u}{\partial t^2} `], [` \dfrac{\partial^2 u}{\partial s \partial t} `] and [` \dfrac{\partial^2 u}{\partial t \partial s} `]  in terms of other "intermediate" partials and evaluate them at [` (0,0) `].

[` \dfrac{\partial^2 u}{\partial t^2}(0,0) = `] [________]{Real(2)}

[` \dfrac{\partial^2 u}{\partial s \partial t}(0,0) = `] [________]{Real(3)}

[` \dfrac{\partial^2 u}{\partial t \partial s}(0,0) = `] [________]{Real(3)}
END_PGML

################################################################
#
#  Answers

$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;
BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION


[` \dfrac{\partial^2 u}{\partial s^2}(0,0) = 2 `] and [` \dfrac{\partial^2 u}{\partial t^2}(0,0) = 2 `] and [` \dfrac{\partial^2 u}{\partial s\partial t}(0,0) = 3 `]. In general,

>>[@ image("f3-worksheet-q5-answer-1.png", width=>500) @]*<<

>>[@ image("f3-worksheet-q5-answer-2.png", width=>500) @]*<<
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();